00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.880
Okay. So, let me talk
a little bit about culture.

00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:57.290
Again, we take it super

00:03:57.291 --> 00:04:00.395
seriously and we talk
about it all the time,

00:04:00.396 --> 00:04:02.870
and the connection to reliability

00:04:02.871 --> 00:04:06.065
is clear that monocultures
are risky, right?

00:04:06.066 --> 00:04:08.075
Monocultures people believe in

00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:09.425
the same vision and

00:04:09.426 --> 00:04:11.740
they agree with each other
and they get it wrong,

00:04:11.741 --> 00:04:14.195
and I've seen it again and again.

00:04:14.196 --> 00:04:19.755
Diversity in our team
delivers creativity,

00:04:19.756 --> 00:04:21.520
innovation, and lowers risk.

00:04:21.521 --> 00:04:25.520
So, yeah, I talk about
diversity all the time.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:31.170
We have a long ways to
go in our industry,

00:04:31.171 --> 00:04:34.130
but also the encouraging thing

00:04:34.131 --> 00:04:35.465
is we're putting a focus on it.

00:04:35.466 --> 00:04:36.770
So, for example, when

00:04:36.771 --> 00:04:41.000
we spin up new teams
and new initiatives,

00:04:41.001 --> 00:04:44.990
we'd set as a target 40
percent diverse hires,

00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:46.355
and we hit it.

00:04:46.356 --> 00:04:50.310
So, we can do it and it's great,

00:04:50.311 --> 00:04:51.950
it's working out for us.

00:04:51.951 --> 00:04:54.020
We're not there yet, we're
trying to get better,

00:04:54.021 --> 00:04:56.745
but wanted to give
you that update.

