we did this network firmware

00:23:29.271 --> 00:23:30.750
because they wanted
greater control,

00:23:30.751 --> 00:23:33.750
we wanted to improve reliability,

00:23:33.751 --> 00:23:35.655
and we wanted to take care
of all the bugs themselves.

00:23:35.656 --> 00:23:38.660
We wanted just the features
we needed to improve

00:23:38.661 --> 00:23:42.000
reliability but let's now
think about the big network.

00:23:42.001 --> 00:23:46.100
Let's think, how do
we build a network

00:23:46.101 --> 00:23:50.905
that is reliable by design
and meet these goals,

00:23:50.906 --> 00:23:52.340
changes work as intended,

00:23:52.341 --> 00:23:56.885
is resilient, we minimize
the impact of changes,

00:23:56.886 --> 00:23:59.945
it learns and adapts
automatically,

00:23:59.946 --> 00:24:03.970
and we can verify
with formal methods

00:24:03.971 --> 00:24:06.390
any gap between what we intend

00:24:06.391 --> 00:24:09.070
the network to do and
what it actually does.

00:24:09.071 --> 00:24:10.590
You saw all those links there,

00:24:10.591 --> 00:24:12.620
there could be little
defects in the optics,

00:24:12.621 --> 00:24:15.130
we have to be able to detect
these little defects.

00:24:15.131 --> 00:24:16.850
Needle in a haystack
type problems

00:24:16.851 --> 00:24:18.565
where we use machine learning.

