So, one theme that I want to

00:26:23.041 --> 00:26:25.700
convey is that a lot
of the stuff we do in

00:26:25.701 --> 00:26:29.100
networking to make the network

00:26:29.101 --> 00:26:33.200
reliable is stuff that you
cannot do without a Cloud.

00:26:33.201 --> 00:26:37.660
The amount of hours and
the computational methods we

00:26:37.661 --> 00:26:42.310
apply are Cloud methods and
we need VM hours to do this.

00:26:42.311 --> 00:26:45.125
So, we simulate-
these are modeling,

00:26:45.126 --> 00:26:48.510
like math models simulations
of the network

00:26:48.511 --> 00:26:50.710
covering literally millions of

00:26:50.711 --> 00:26:53.070
contingencies for every fiber

00:26:53.071 --> 00:26:54.180
of things that could go wrong,

00:26:54.181 --> 00:26:57.290
there's a pipeline
here and timelines.

00:26:57.291 --> 00:27:01.015
So, think about if you use Azure,

00:27:01.016 --> 00:27:03.170
you're running Azure Batch
every time you think of

00:27:03.171 --> 00:27:05.850
a project and you pretty much,

00:27:05.851 --> 00:27:08.330
and this is what
the Cloud job is all about,

00:27:08.331 --> 00:27:09.750
you try to anticipate

00:27:09.751 --> 00:27:12.610
all the things that
could possibly go wrong.

00:27:12.611 --> 00:27:16.390
Get that risk into the model and

00:27:16.391 --> 00:27:18.060
then simulate all these things

00:27:18.061 --> 00:27:20.635
and see if you're
resilient to them.

00:27:20.636 --> 00:27:23.530
That's just routine for us.

00:27:23.531 --> 00:27:26.080
We run these simulations
before we touch

00:27:26.081 --> 00:27:30.600
the network and before and
as we design the network.

